1
00:00:09,926 --> 00:00:11,010
Have a nice trip.

2
00:00:33,533 --> 00:00:34,951
CUSTOMS OFFICIAL (MINISTRY OF FINANCE)
MACHI MORI

3
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:37,871
Well then, that wraps up our duties
for today! Great work, everyone!

4
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:39,914
-Good work.
-Good work.

5
00:00:44,878 --> 00:00:46,921
Excuse me, Matsuyama.

6
00:00:48,047 --> 00:00:51,634
You didn't check that last passenger's
luggage. Was that okay?

7
00:00:52,218 --> 00:00:55,805
Oh. Well, nothing seemed
particularly suspicious.

8
00:00:56,681 --> 00:00:59,809
-But…
-You Customs folks take it easy, huh?

9
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:01,728
I've been thinking about this for a while.

10
00:01:01,811 --> 00:01:04,647
You don't check everyone's baggage, right?

11
00:01:04,731 --> 00:01:06,107
Is that acceptable?

12
00:01:06,191 --> 00:01:08,860
True. Are you sure you're not
letting something slip by?

13
00:01:08,943 --> 00:01:12,614
We must always stay focused and observe
carefully, so it doesn't happen.

14
00:01:12,697 --> 00:01:16,910
And when a bag catches our eye,
we examine it thoroughly.

15
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:19,454
We stop suspicious people every day.

16
00:01:19,537 --> 00:01:23,249
Exactly. At Customs,
every single second is a battle.

17
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:25,710
It's not like Immigration,

18
00:01:25,794 --> 00:01:27,837
where you just chat
mindlessly with passengers.

19
00:01:27,921 --> 00:01:31,508
-Chat mindlessly?
-Immigration is so carefree. Sounds nice.

20
00:01:31,591 --> 00:01:33,843
-Could you please not lump us together?
-That's my line.

21
00:01:33,927 --> 00:01:37,514
Well, you know… Anyway, Mori,
was there something about

22
00:01:37,597 --> 00:01:39,974
that last passenger's luggage
that caught your attention?

23
00:01:40,058 --> 00:01:41,392
Yes, very much so.

24
00:01:42,185 --> 00:01:43,645
What was it? Was something wrong?

25
00:01:44,270 --> 00:01:46,648
What are we going to do?
She's already gone through.

26
00:01:47,982 --> 00:01:49,943
The pattern on the front of her bag

27
00:01:52,028 --> 00:01:55,740
was Matyo embroidery.

28
00:01:56,991 --> 00:01:58,159
Matyo embroidery?

29
00:02:00,453 --> 00:02:02,705
It's traditional Hungarian embroidery.

30
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:08,253
It features rounded rose petals
and a striking, vibrant red.

31
00:02:08,336 --> 00:02:11,506
It makes the flowers look almost alive.

32
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:15,260
-Those are roses?
-It certainly is unique.

33
00:02:16,261 --> 00:02:18,304
And? What was suspicious about it?

34
00:02:18,388 --> 00:02:19,973
Oh, nothing in particular.

35
00:02:20,557 --> 00:02:23,518
But I just wanted
to inspect it more closely.

36
00:02:24,936 --> 00:02:27,021
What is wrong with this person?

37
00:02:32,777 --> 00:02:35,071
Yes, this is Gate 24.

38
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:39,576
Customs sure has it tough,
having to appraise embroidery too.

39
00:02:39,659 --> 00:02:41,119
Yes.

40
00:02:41,202 --> 00:02:43,955
Well, anyway, at least today
ended without incident.

41
00:02:44,038 --> 00:02:45,582
Um, um…

42
00:02:48,001 --> 00:02:50,253
T-There's a bomb threat.

43
00:02:51,588 --> 00:02:52,463
It seems.

44
00:02:53,631 --> 00:02:54,632
-What?
-What?

45
00:02:56,551 --> 00:02:58,386
Thank you. Keep us updated.

46
00:03:00,972 --> 00:03:02,348
Airport Director Ikeura.

47
00:03:04,142 --> 00:03:05,643
We just received this phone call.

48
00:03:07,687 --> 00:03:10,565
<i>This is the Kanto International</i>
<i>Airport Information Center.</i>

49
00:03:10,648 --> 00:03:13,860
<i>A bomb has been planted on the flight</i>
<i>bound for Rome International Airport.</i>

50
00:03:14,652 --> 00:03:17,530
-<i>Who is this?</i>
-<i>If you want it disarmed,</i>

51
00:03:17,614 --> 00:03:21,034
<i>prepare three million dollars</i>
<i>by midnight tonight.</i>

52
00:03:21,117 --> 00:03:23,578
<i>I repeat, a bomb has been planted</i>
<i>on the flight bound</i>

53
00:03:23,661 --> 00:03:25,538
<i>for Rome International Airport.</i>

54
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:29,542
It could be a prank,
but we can't afford to ignore it.

55
00:03:29,626 --> 00:03:31,169
We are currently coordinating

56
00:03:31,252 --> 00:03:33,212
with security companies and the police.

57
00:03:34,589 --> 00:03:39,093
Bound for Rome…
Today, the only flight is EUW301.

58
00:03:39,177 --> 00:03:41,429
Yes. The flight cannot take off

59
00:03:41,512 --> 00:03:42,722
until safety checks are done.

60
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:44,557
The passengers on this flight

61
00:03:44,641 --> 00:03:47,018
will need to be rebooked
on flights tomorrow or later.

62
00:03:47,101 --> 00:03:50,313
Then we will handle
those passengers at Gate 24.

63
00:03:50,396 --> 00:03:52,565
No, no, we'll handle them
at the main booth.

64
00:03:53,149 --> 00:03:55,276
In an emergency like this,
we'll have a backup booth--

65
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:58,112
We will handle them.

66
00:03:59,572 --> 00:04:00,448
Okay.

67
00:04:09,249 --> 00:04:10,083
TIME TILL DETONATION: 4 HOURS

68
00:04:10,166 --> 00:04:14,462
Due to a bomb threat, Flight EUW301
has been canceled for today.

69
00:04:15,713 --> 00:04:18,299
The 23 transit passengers
scheduled for this flight

70
00:04:18,383 --> 00:04:20,551
will temporarily enter Japan.

71
00:04:20,635 --> 00:04:24,222
These 23 individuals
are subject to strict inspection.

72
00:04:24,305 --> 00:04:26,432
We're handling that?

73
00:04:26,516 --> 00:04:29,060
So this time, we need
to inspect everyone's luggage.

74
00:04:29,936 --> 00:04:31,896
We need to check thoroughly
for explosives.

75
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:34,148
Swiftly and carefully, right?

76
00:04:34,232 --> 00:04:35,483
Precisely.

77
00:04:36,234 --> 00:04:39,404
To avoid panic, we haven't informed
the passengers about the bomb threat,

78
00:04:39,487 --> 00:04:42,156
and flights other than this one
are operating as normal.

79
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:45,159
What if a bomb is found?

80
00:04:45,243 --> 00:04:47,620
At that point,
all flights might be canceled.

81
00:04:47,704 --> 00:04:50,415
Prepare for every possible scenario.

82
00:04:50,498 --> 00:04:53,084
I'm heading
to the Crisis Management Center now.

83
00:04:58,631 --> 00:05:00,008
Don't panic.

84
00:05:00,091 --> 00:05:01,759
What you need
to do is the same as always.

85
00:05:02,343 --> 00:05:04,929
Pass who should pass,
and stop who should be stopped.

86
00:05:05,763 --> 00:05:07,682
And objects, too.

87
00:05:10,101 --> 00:05:11,561
Pass the objects that should pass,

88
00:05:12,145 --> 00:05:14,522
and stop the objects
that should be stopped.

89
00:05:14,605 --> 00:05:15,898
Exactly.

90
00:05:17,025 --> 00:05:18,568
Make sure to carefully evaluate

91
00:05:20,028 --> 00:05:21,738
both people and objects.

92
00:05:21,821 --> 00:05:22,655
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

93
00:05:22,739 --> 00:05:24,198
All right, let's go, go, go.

94
00:05:26,117 --> 00:05:28,286
FLIGHT CANCELED

95
00:05:32,248 --> 00:05:33,791
Ah, Machi!

96
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:35,376
-Chika.
-We'll talk later.

97
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:37,378
I brought the passengers.

98
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:54,312
This is a problem.

99
00:05:54,395 --> 00:05:57,065
I have an important
business meeting tomorrow.

100
00:05:57,148 --> 00:05:58,858
If I don't fly tonight, I won't make it.

101
00:05:59,484 --> 00:06:01,736
We are truly sorry for the inconvenience.

102
00:06:01,819 --> 00:06:03,988
What are you going to do
if my deal falls through?

103
00:06:04,072 --> 00:06:05,364
You'll owe me damages!

104
00:06:05,448 --> 00:06:08,159
We will arrange
for a later departure date.

105
00:06:08,242 --> 00:06:11,496
Why are we even being brought
all the way out here in the first place?

106
00:06:11,579 --> 00:06:12,705
Where are we?

107
00:06:12,789 --> 00:06:14,373
Man…

108
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:15,875
This never happened to me before!

109
00:06:15,958 --> 00:06:16,876
Shall we go help?

110
00:06:19,087 --> 00:06:20,171
Enough with the apologies…

111
00:06:22,048 --> 00:06:22,882
‎What?

112
00:06:24,383 --> 00:06:26,677
Handling complaints
isn't in my jurisdiction.

113
00:06:27,887 --> 00:06:30,473
That might be true, but…

114
00:06:30,556 --> 00:06:31,766
What is this place?

115
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:33,935
When are we going to fly?

116
00:06:37,146 --> 00:06:38,689
What's wrong with you?

117
00:06:44,195 --> 00:06:46,114
-How many hours are we gonna wait?
-Are you hurt?

118
00:06:48,533 --> 00:06:49,992
‎We are still confriming...

119
00:06:50,076 --> 00:06:53,121
Please calm down.
Getting angry won't help anything.

120
00:06:53,204 --> 00:06:54,038
Huh?

121
00:06:54,122 --> 00:06:56,499
My whole life depends on this flight!

122
00:06:56,582 --> 00:06:59,043
-You're not the only one in a tough spot.
-Here you go.

123
00:06:59,127 --> 00:07:00,044
-Thank you.
-They are doing

124
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:01,462
their best to handle the situation!

125
00:07:01,546 --> 00:07:03,548
So what? I'm a customer here!

126
00:07:03,631 --> 00:07:04,966
I'm a customer too.

127
00:07:05,049 --> 00:07:08,219
So is everyone else here.
So is this couple.

128
00:07:08,302 --> 00:07:10,304
All these passengers
are having trouble right now.

129
00:07:10,388 --> 00:07:13,057
Because of you, no one can hear
the explanations or get their luggage.

130
00:07:30,366 --> 00:07:31,868
-Thank you very much.
-It's okay.

131
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:54,557
TOKYO METROPOLITAN POLICE

132
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,225
-Call in.
-Roger.

133
00:07:59,353 --> 00:08:02,273
First floor passageway, all clear.

134
00:08:02,356 --> 00:08:04,692
Roger, please continue to search.

135
00:08:04,775 --> 00:08:07,320
<i>Please look into this one more time.</i>

136
00:08:07,403 --> 00:08:08,571
<i>Nothing abnormal at the moment.</i>

137
00:08:08,654 --> 00:08:09,947
<i>Currently checking.</i>

138
00:08:10,031 --> 00:08:12,325
-Excuse me.
-Hello.

139
00:08:12,992 --> 00:08:13,951
‎I'm from Section 1, MPD.

140
00:08:14,327 --> 00:08:15,369
So?

141
00:08:52,990 --> 00:08:57,161
But I hurt my leg right before we left.

142
00:08:57,245 --> 00:09:00,831
Oh, that's unfortunate.
Please, don't force yourself.

143
00:09:06,379 --> 00:09:07,713
What is this?

144
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:10,633
It's my husband's. He loves crafting.

145
00:09:10,716 --> 00:09:15,137
Oh my… By any chance,
did he craft that pendant as well?

146
00:09:15,721 --> 00:09:17,223
Oh, yes.

147
00:09:19,308 --> 00:09:22,061
It's lovely. That pretty lady
in the photograph…

148
00:09:22,144 --> 00:09:23,771
Is she your daughter?

149
00:09:23,854 --> 00:09:25,231
Yes, that's Emma.

150
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:33,990
Our only child. She's been
performing in Norway these days.

151
00:09:34,073 --> 00:09:37,368
-Amazing! She's a professional violinist.
-Yes.

152
00:09:42,206 --> 00:09:44,458
-Natori, could you take over for a moment?
-Yes.

153
00:09:45,167 --> 00:09:46,252
Just a moment, please.

154
00:09:51,757 --> 00:09:52,925
The police?

155
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:55,136
Hello. Is something the matter?

156
00:09:55,219 --> 00:09:56,929
No, just a quick check.

157
00:09:57,013 --> 00:09:58,264
Please don't mind us.

158
00:09:58,347 --> 00:10:00,474
The bomb threat, right?
Do you have information on the suspect--

159
00:10:00,558 --> 00:10:02,685
I told you, don't worry about it.

160
00:10:11,235 --> 00:10:12,862
-Everything all right?
-Yes.

161
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:14,614
How about the luggage?

162
00:10:14,697 --> 00:10:17,450
-No issues--
-Um…

163
00:10:17,533 --> 00:10:19,118
About this…

164
00:10:19,869 --> 00:10:23,289
Mori, I know you like things
like embroidery, but not here!

165
00:10:24,624 --> 00:10:25,708
Everything is fine.

166
00:10:27,585 --> 00:10:29,378
Please, go ahead.

167
00:10:30,004 --> 00:10:30,921
Here you are.

168
00:10:33,132 --> 00:10:33,966
‎Thank you.

169
00:10:35,009 --> 00:10:36,218
Take care.

170
00:10:44,352 --> 00:10:45,436
All right.

171
00:10:48,314 --> 00:10:49,899
What did the police want?

172
00:10:49,982 --> 00:10:52,026
They wouldn't tell me anything.

173
00:10:52,109 --> 00:10:53,903
What? What's that about?

174
00:10:53,986 --> 00:10:57,740
Again? Times like this are when
we should be sharing information.

175
00:10:58,407 --> 00:10:59,742
Next, please.

176
00:10:59,825 --> 00:11:01,577
-Passport, please.
-Yes.

177
00:11:06,248 --> 00:11:07,291
Your luggage, please.

178
00:11:07,917 --> 00:11:09,502
May I check your luggage?

179
00:11:12,171 --> 00:11:13,130
Go ahead.

180
00:11:14,632 --> 00:11:17,885
I'm only staying in Japan overnight,
but I'm still getting checked, huh?

181
00:11:17,968 --> 00:11:19,887
My apologies. This is a security check.

182
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:21,389
LEFT FINGERPRINT
RIGHT FINGERPRINT

183
00:11:24,892 --> 00:11:25,893
Could you come here?

184
00:11:26,644 --> 00:11:27,686
‎Yes.

185
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:30,398
-Sakura Nakae, right?
-Yes.

186
00:11:30,481 --> 00:11:32,983
You currently reside
in the Republic of Lorishika.

187
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:35,236
What is your occupation?

188
00:11:35,319 --> 00:11:37,488
I teach at a Japanese language school.

189
00:11:37,571 --> 00:11:40,199
-How long have you been there?
-About three years.

190
00:11:40,950 --> 00:11:43,202
Before that, I taught
in a few other countries.

191
00:11:44,578 --> 00:11:45,788
Is there a problem?

192
00:11:47,373 --> 00:11:48,582
Please wait a moment.

193
00:11:48,666 --> 00:11:50,084
SAKURA NAKAE

194
00:12:00,094 --> 00:12:00,928
DUST-FREE CHALK

195
00:12:01,011 --> 00:12:03,347
Thank you for waiting.
The luggage is all clear?

196
00:12:04,432 --> 00:12:05,766
Oh, yes.

197
00:12:06,851 --> 00:12:07,810
KANTO 26/6/2009

198
00:12:07,893 --> 00:12:09,520
Here you are.

199
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:11,981
May I?

200
00:12:12,064 --> 00:12:13,524
-Yes, there's no problem.
-Okay.

201
00:12:15,484 --> 00:12:18,612
What was that about just now?
You were looking something up.

202
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:24,034
I can't tell you.
That's Immigration information.

203
00:12:24,118 --> 00:12:26,912
Hey, didn't we decide earlier

204
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:29,665
that we should share
information within the team?

205
00:12:30,875 --> 00:12:33,252
I decide what gets shared from here.

206
00:12:33,335 --> 00:12:36,422
Now, now, as long as there
wasn't a problem, it's okay, right?

207
00:12:36,505 --> 00:12:39,383
-We've safely sent off all the passengers.
-Right.

208
00:12:39,467 --> 00:12:41,469
No, there's still one person left.

209
00:12:41,552 --> 00:12:42,386
-What?
-What?

210
00:12:44,388 --> 00:12:45,681
That one…

211
00:13:02,490 --> 00:13:05,117
Excuse me. Please step up for processing.

212
00:13:05,201 --> 00:13:07,286
-No, I'm fine.
-Pardon?

213
00:13:07,953 --> 00:13:10,664
Even if I get out of here,
I'm flying tomorrow anyway, right?

214
00:13:10,748 --> 00:13:12,917
Going back and forth is a waste of effort.

215
00:13:13,542 --> 00:13:16,253
I'll just spend the night here.

216
00:13:17,338 --> 00:13:20,174
I have no intention
of going through immigration.

217
00:13:24,762 --> 00:13:26,180
Oh my…

218
00:13:26,263 --> 00:13:27,723
<i>Please continue your search.</i>

219
00:13:27,806 --> 00:13:29,725
-<i>I'll confirm from here.</i>
-<i>No issues found.</i>

220
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:32,895
So far, no suspicious objects
have been found.

221
00:13:32,978 --> 00:13:37,107
The caller said to prepare three million
dollars by midnight, correct?

222
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:41,445
Yes. Still, preparing that
much cash in this timeframe…

223
00:13:42,112 --> 00:13:44,198
Counselor, can't you do
something about it?

224
00:13:44,823 --> 00:13:47,785
If I had such convenient authority,
I would have used it already.

225
00:13:49,495 --> 00:13:50,788
How does the culprit

226
00:13:51,580 --> 00:13:54,250
plan to receive the money?

227
00:13:54,333 --> 00:13:55,751
Who knows?

228
00:13:55,834 --> 00:13:58,212
There's been no further contact.

229
00:13:58,963 --> 00:14:03,008
Excuse me, sir. This is a restricted area.

230
00:14:03,092 --> 00:14:05,427
In any case,
we can't have you staying here.

231
00:14:05,511 --> 00:14:06,470
That's right.

232
00:14:07,638 --> 00:14:08,889
Sir?

233
00:14:09,515 --> 00:14:11,725
We really do understand how you feel.

234
00:14:11,809 --> 00:14:14,395
Would you like some help moving?

235
00:14:14,478 --> 00:14:19,358
We just need a moment, no,
a minute to check your luggage and--

236
00:14:19,441 --> 00:14:21,986
-All right, fine! You're so annoying.
-Thank you.

237
00:14:22,069 --> 00:14:25,114
-Thank goodness.
-Thank you very much.

238
00:14:25,197 --> 00:14:27,658
Please, go ahead.

239
00:14:28,868 --> 00:14:31,036
Thank you very much.

240
00:14:36,041 --> 00:14:37,418
Passport, please.

241
00:14:47,052 --> 00:14:49,346
-Go ahead.
-I'll check your luggage here.

242
00:14:59,023 --> 00:14:59,982
Thank you.

243
00:15:00,065 --> 00:15:01,692
Satoru Soma, right?

244
00:15:02,693 --> 00:15:03,569
What is your profession?

245
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:09,491
Trading. I handle
infrastructure projects overseas.

246
00:15:10,326 --> 00:15:13,037
-That sounds like a respectable job.
-Doesn't it?

247
00:15:27,343 --> 00:15:30,596
-Something wrong?
-Oh, no…

248
00:15:32,932 --> 00:15:34,266
Do you have a moment?

249
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:40,522
Mr. Soma.

250
00:15:42,524 --> 00:15:44,109
Regarding this item in your luggage…

251
00:15:59,124 --> 00:16:02,544
Sorry to keep you waiting.
How are things on the Immigration side?

252
00:16:03,379 --> 00:16:06,548
-No particular issues.
-Customs has no issues either then.

253
00:16:07,299 --> 00:16:08,133
‎Huh?

254
00:16:18,894 --> 00:16:20,104
Please, go ahead.

255
00:16:26,902 --> 00:16:28,153
What was that about?

256
00:16:28,737 --> 00:16:30,614
Was there a problem with that passenger?

257
00:16:31,448 --> 00:16:34,493
I can't say. That's Customs information.

258
00:16:34,576 --> 00:16:37,329
Wait, now Customs is doing it too?

259
00:16:37,413 --> 00:16:39,623
Didn't you say we should
share information?

260
00:16:41,792 --> 00:16:45,921
Then you tell me about that woman earlier.

261
00:16:47,339 --> 00:16:49,925
It feels like both Immigration
and Customs are so secretive.

262
00:16:50,884 --> 00:16:52,177
And the police too.

263
00:16:56,223 --> 00:16:58,559
Like I said, the flight isn't taking off!

264
00:16:59,393 --> 00:17:03,522
Can't you negotiate with them and somehow
push back tomorrow's meeting?

265
00:17:04,732 --> 00:17:05,691
Yes.

266
00:17:06,650 --> 00:17:08,485
I don't know yet.

267
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:13,532
Thirty minutes left…

268
00:17:14,241 --> 00:17:15,909
I hope nothing happens.

269
00:17:15,993 --> 00:17:17,202
‎TIME TILL DETONATION: 30 MINUTES

270
00:17:17,286 --> 00:17:18,871
Um…

271
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:24,418
Why was tonight's flight to Rome
targeted in the first place?

272
00:17:27,004 --> 00:17:28,130
Don't ask me.

273
00:17:28,213 --> 00:17:30,257
I was wondering about that too.

274
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:35,679
If the perpetrator's goal were political,
there would usually be a clear message.

275
00:17:35,763 --> 00:17:38,098
It doesn't feel like that.

276
00:17:38,182 --> 00:17:42,352
Alternatively, if it were for money,
why not say there's a bomb in the airport?

277
00:17:42,436 --> 00:17:44,563
A wider-scale threat
would be more effective.

278
00:17:44,646 --> 00:17:46,023
It's strange.

279
00:17:46,982 --> 00:17:47,983
I see.

280
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:54,198
I assumed there was some
significance to this specific airplane.

281
00:17:54,782 --> 00:17:56,325
-Significance?
-Yes.

282
00:17:56,408 --> 00:17:58,577
Though I don't know what it is yet.

283
00:17:58,660 --> 00:18:00,037
That's interesting.

284
00:18:00,913 --> 00:18:02,372
Even facing the same event,

285
00:18:02,456 --> 00:18:06,710
Hayami looks at the people
while Mori looks at the objects.

286
00:18:06,794 --> 00:18:08,754
The difference between
Immigration and Customs.

287
00:18:08,837 --> 00:18:11,548
No, no, we think about people too.

288
00:18:12,633 --> 00:18:14,718
Mori is just very unique.

289
00:18:16,303 --> 00:18:19,556
Why this specific plane, huh…

290
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:21,767
FLIGHT NAMES

291
00:18:21,850 --> 00:18:22,935
Mr. Fukasawa.

292
00:18:25,187 --> 00:18:26,647
Hello, everyone.

293
00:18:28,232 --> 00:18:29,066
Sit down, sit down.

294
00:18:33,654 --> 00:18:34,863
What's the situation?

295
00:18:38,033 --> 00:18:40,160
No bomb has been found.

296
00:18:44,164 --> 00:18:46,125
Really?

297
00:18:48,418 --> 00:18:51,505
It's just like the incident
five years ago.

298
00:18:52,381 --> 00:18:53,215
Five years ago?

299
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:59,596
A call came into this airport claiming
a bomb was planted on a certain flight.

300
00:19:01,056 --> 00:19:04,560
-What happened?
-The flights that day were canceled.

301
00:19:05,394 --> 00:19:07,104
No bomb was found, though.

302
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:08,939
What a terrible prank.

303
00:19:09,022 --> 00:19:11,775
So something like that happened
before I started working here.

304
00:19:11,859 --> 00:19:13,152
I didn't even know,

305
00:19:13,235 --> 00:19:16,989
-and I know everything!
-To prevent copycats,

306
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:19,992
few people knew about that case.

307
00:19:20,075 --> 00:19:22,786
It really is similar to this case.

308
00:19:24,079 --> 00:19:25,539
Could it be a coincidence?

309
00:19:30,252 --> 00:19:31,628
Yes, this is Gate 24.

310
00:19:32,754 --> 00:19:34,089
Oh, yes.

311
00:19:34,173 --> 00:19:35,090
-Open the door!
-Iuchi?

312
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:36,425
Open the door!

313
00:19:36,508 --> 00:19:37,801
I'm coming! Come in.

314
00:19:37,885 --> 00:19:40,429
-What's wrong?
-Do you know where that couple went?

315
00:19:40,512 --> 00:19:43,098
-The couple?
-Did something happen?

316
00:19:43,182 --> 00:19:45,142
Um, that was ground staff.

317
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:46,643
Several passengers who passed through

318
00:19:46,727 --> 00:19:48,770
the booth earlier
haven't arrived at the hotel yet.

319
00:19:49,771 --> 00:19:54,359
Sakura Nakae, Satoru Soma,
and Mr. Josef and Mrs. Luisa Meyer.

320
00:19:54,443 --> 00:19:55,485
That's it, that couple.

321
00:19:55,569 --> 00:19:56,820
Why those four?

322
00:19:56,904 --> 00:19:59,406
This is really bad, isn't it?

323
00:19:59,489 --> 00:20:00,616
There's barely any time left.

324
00:20:03,744 --> 00:20:07,831
<i>A suspicious object has been</i>
<i>discovered inside the airport.</i>

325
00:20:07,915 --> 00:20:11,001
Over there, that wasn't there
during the day.

326
00:20:11,835 --> 00:20:14,338
North hallway beside the mall area!

327
00:20:14,963 --> 00:20:17,174
Suspicious object found.

328
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:20,010
-It was real after all?
-I repeat.

329
00:20:20,093 --> 00:20:22,804
Suspicious object found.
Currently examining it.

330
00:20:22,888 --> 00:20:24,848
-Roger.
-<i>Update from the scene.</i>

331
00:20:24,932 --> 00:20:25,807
Yes.

332
00:20:25,891 --> 00:20:26,767
‎MALL AREA

333
00:20:26,850 --> 00:20:29,144
<i>The suspicious object is a hard case,</i>

334
00:20:29,228 --> 00:20:33,106
<i>color is black, plastic handle,</i>
<i>currently on its side.</i>

335
00:20:33,190 --> 00:20:36,151
No, you all can't hear this.

336
00:20:36,235 --> 00:20:37,486
-Hey, let's go.
-Okay!

337
00:20:40,072 --> 00:20:41,114
Mori?

338
00:20:46,161 --> 00:20:47,037
TOKYO POLICE - KEEP OUT

339
00:20:53,001 --> 00:20:55,295
-Where is it?
-Around that pole?

340
00:20:55,379 --> 00:20:57,089
‎Hello.

341
00:20:58,131 --> 00:20:59,800
-That girl…
-Wait!

342
00:20:59,883 --> 00:21:00,842
Wait, Machi!

343
00:21:00,926 --> 00:21:03,387
Hey, what are you doing? Get back!

344
00:21:05,472 --> 00:21:06,807
It's almost time.

345
00:21:10,894 --> 00:21:13,605
What? Um…

346
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:15,983
-That's, um…
-You can't be here.

347
00:21:17,067 --> 00:21:18,735
-Mori!
-Ten seconds left.

348
00:21:21,113 --> 00:21:23,824
That's Soma's suitcase.

349
00:21:24,658 --> 00:21:27,119
I checked the contents
at the gate earlier.

350
00:21:30,914 --> 00:21:31,999
Get down!

351
00:21:38,880 --> 00:21:40,215
MPD - KEEP OUT

352
00:21:41,049 --> 00:21:42,301
Huh?

353
00:21:45,220 --> 00:21:47,556
-The bomb…
-Yes?

354
00:21:49,141 --> 00:21:50,392
is not in there.

355
00:21:51,393 --> 00:21:52,769
-What?
-Right?

356
00:21:52,853 --> 00:21:53,812
Yes.

357
00:21:55,814 --> 00:21:59,735
-But why was it in a place like that?
-Excuse me, excuse me.

358
00:21:59,818 --> 00:22:02,070
Where have you all been?

359
00:22:02,154 --> 00:22:04,531
Oh, Josef.

360
00:22:04,614 --> 00:22:06,450
Perfect timing.

361
00:22:06,533 --> 00:22:09,870
He said he lost his bag,
so we were helping him look for it.

362
00:22:11,371 --> 00:22:13,165
Ah, that's mine!

363
00:22:13,957 --> 00:22:19,004
-Hey, wait, wait!
-Stop! It's dangerous!

364
00:22:19,087 --> 00:22:19,963
‎ARRIVALS LOBBY

365
00:22:20,047 --> 00:22:22,841
It appears the passenger
was a victim of theft.

366
00:22:22,924 --> 00:22:25,427
-Who is this person?
-We're still investigating.

367
00:22:25,510 --> 00:22:29,389
But they don't appear clearly
in other footage either.

368
00:22:33,185 --> 00:22:37,147
In the end, there was no bomb anywhere.

369
00:22:37,230 --> 00:22:39,608
Yes. No contact from
the perpetrator either.

370
00:22:39,691 --> 00:22:42,736
The police suspect
it was a malicious prank.

371
00:22:42,819 --> 00:22:44,988
Whose fault is this, damn it?!

372
00:22:48,825 --> 00:22:52,245
I saw a lot of police officers
out there earlier.

373
00:22:52,329 --> 00:22:54,289
That was, well…

374
00:22:54,372 --> 00:22:56,792
Was there a bomb scare or something?

375
00:22:57,918 --> 00:23:00,003
Ah, my apologies.

376
00:23:00,629 --> 00:23:03,548
You all just look so tense.

377
00:23:03,632 --> 00:23:06,176
No, no, there's no need to worry.

378
00:23:06,259 --> 00:23:08,762
But still, you're as sharp as ever.

379
00:23:08,845 --> 00:23:11,014
A bomb scare?

380
00:23:11,598 --> 00:23:13,517
It's probably just a prank by someone.

381
00:23:14,768 --> 00:23:16,228
Why do you think it was a prank?

382
00:23:17,187 --> 00:23:18,021
Huh?

383
00:23:18,105 --> 00:23:20,524
I was just guessing.

384
00:23:20,607 --> 00:23:23,527
More importantly,
catch the criminal, quickly!

385
00:23:23,610 --> 00:23:27,614
We'd like to ask you some details.
Would you all mind joining as well?

386
00:23:27,697 --> 00:23:28,865
Sure.

387
00:23:28,949 --> 00:23:31,660
Well then, we'll see you later.

388
00:23:38,542 --> 00:23:39,417
Iuchi.

389
00:23:41,503 --> 00:23:44,965
Earlier, you told Josef
he was as sharp as ever, right?

390
00:23:45,048 --> 00:23:47,884
I was curious about that too.
What did you mean by that?

391
00:23:49,052 --> 00:23:51,096
What were the police investigating?

392
00:23:52,305 --> 00:23:54,432
Who exactly is Josef?

393
00:23:58,103 --> 00:23:59,604
Um…

394
00:24:04,276 --> 00:24:07,904
This badge was in the Meyers' luggage.

395
00:24:07,988 --> 00:24:12,534
It's awarded to distinguished personnel
in the Ordania Police Department, right?

396
00:24:13,034 --> 00:24:15,662
<i>And for high-ranking officials, no less.</i>

397
00:24:16,246 --> 00:24:17,455
Is this supposed to be a badge?

398
00:24:18,373 --> 00:24:21,459
Mori, you really know
everything, don't you?

399
00:24:21,543 --> 00:24:23,003
Oh, no, it was just by chance.

400
00:24:23,086 --> 00:24:24,254
Is that really something
you just happen to know?

401
00:24:24,337 --> 00:24:28,216
So, Josef is a former high-ranking officer
of the Ordania Police?

402
00:24:31,970 --> 00:24:33,722
-Oh, iced coffee.
-No, it's hot.

403
00:24:34,764 --> 00:24:37,100
Well, we've collaborated
with him a few times

404
00:24:37,184 --> 00:24:39,019
<i>on international crime investigations.</i>

405
00:24:39,102 --> 00:24:41,479
<i>When we heard he was among</i>
<i>the passengers today,</i>

406
00:24:41,563 --> 00:24:44,065
we were instructed from above
to treat him with utmost respect.

407
00:24:44,691 --> 00:24:47,235
What? So it was just VIP treatment?

408
00:24:47,319 --> 00:24:49,821
-Huh?
-No, no, VIP treatment is important.

409
00:24:49,905 --> 00:24:51,239
I see.

410
00:24:51,907 --> 00:24:54,618
So that's why it was kept secret.

411
00:24:54,701 --> 00:24:57,287
By the way, both Immigration
and Customs are hiding something.

412
00:24:57,954 --> 00:25:00,957
That's right. It's time you told us!

413
00:25:02,209 --> 00:25:03,460
Did something happen?

414
00:25:06,338 --> 00:25:07,589
Okay…

415
00:25:09,257 --> 00:25:10,967
About Sakura Nakae…

416
00:25:11,635 --> 00:25:15,972
She has a past record
of being detained by foreign authorities.

417
00:25:16,056 --> 00:25:18,475
<i>It seems she worked a side job</i>
<i>in nightlife entertainment.</i>

418
00:25:18,558 --> 00:25:22,395
<i>However, the severity was low, and it is</i>
<i>unrelated to her current situation.</i>

419
00:25:22,479 --> 00:25:26,441
Above all, since it concerns her privacy,

420
00:25:26,524 --> 00:25:28,944
I believed it shouldn't
be shared recklessly.

421
00:25:29,527 --> 00:25:32,113
I see. That's true.

422
00:25:32,197 --> 00:25:34,741
It might not be something
to go around telling people.

423
00:25:34,824 --> 00:25:38,119
As expected of you, Mr. Hayami.
I thought as much.

424
00:25:38,954 --> 00:25:41,081
And what about Customs?

425
00:25:43,917 --> 00:25:46,127
Regarding Soma, inside his luggage…

426
00:25:48,922 --> 00:25:50,924
-there was a magazine.
-A magazine?

427
00:25:51,967 --> 00:25:54,678
An adult magazine. Uncensored.

428
00:25:58,807 --> 00:26:03,019
So that means… In other words…

429
00:26:03,103 --> 00:26:04,729
A porno-mag, right?

430
00:26:05,939 --> 00:26:09,818
It might be fine overseas, but it's not
allowed to be brought into Japan.

431
00:26:10,485 --> 00:26:14,030
<i>So that's why he was reluctant</i>
<i>to go through processing!</i>

432
00:26:14,114 --> 00:26:16,199
The magazine was confiscated.

433
00:26:16,283 --> 00:26:20,453
But since this also
concerned a passenger's privacy…

434
00:26:21,204 --> 00:26:22,789
So that's what it was.

435
00:26:22,872 --> 00:26:27,877
In the end, everyone was acting
out of consideration for the passengers.

436
00:26:27,961 --> 00:26:33,425
With different positions
and responsibilities, sharing information

437
00:26:34,009 --> 00:26:35,468
can be quite challenging.

438
00:26:46,313 --> 00:26:47,772
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

439
00:26:48,315 --> 00:26:49,190
Thank you very much.

440
00:26:50,233 --> 00:26:53,695
Counselor, the task force is dissolved.

441
00:26:53,778 --> 00:26:56,197
The passengers from that flight
will be rebooked

442
00:26:56,281 --> 00:26:58,116
on an early morning temporary flight.

443
00:26:59,784 --> 00:27:00,952
Still working on something?

444
00:27:01,036 --> 00:27:05,206
Five years ago, there was
a similar commotion, wasn't there?

445
00:27:06,541 --> 00:27:08,585
That was a real nuisance.

446
00:27:09,627 --> 00:27:10,503
What about it?

447
00:27:12,672 --> 00:27:14,966
Do you have detailed records?

448
00:27:24,309 --> 00:27:26,519
This way, please.
We will take you to the hotel.

449
00:27:28,104 --> 00:27:29,356
May I go as well?

450
00:27:30,190 --> 00:27:31,816
Yes, and Soma, if you'd like.

451
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:34,652
Of course! I went through a nightmare.

452
00:27:35,278 --> 00:27:37,781
Well, I'll let it slide this time.

453
00:27:38,782 --> 00:27:41,868
Actually, I just got good news.

454
00:27:41,951 --> 00:27:44,871
Today's business meeting
has been postponed.

455
00:27:46,039 --> 00:27:49,626
A lot happened,
but all's well that ends well.

456
00:27:53,671 --> 00:27:54,589
Thank you.

457
00:27:57,133 --> 00:27:59,594
Nakatsuka, let's load the luggage.

458
00:28:00,678 --> 00:28:01,805
I'll take this for you.

459
00:28:04,015 --> 00:28:05,600
Hey, what are you doing?

460
00:28:05,683 --> 00:28:07,477
-I'm very sorry!
-Sorry.

461
00:28:19,489 --> 00:28:22,033
-Is this everything?
-Yes. Thank you very much.

462
00:28:22,992 --> 00:28:26,371
-Are you sure? Is there any other…
-It's fine now, really.

463
00:28:27,664 --> 00:28:29,791
-Okay.
-Pardon us.

464
00:28:31,626 --> 00:28:33,378
Let me help you.

465
00:28:33,461 --> 00:28:36,506
Oh, I'm good, thank you. I'm very good.

466
00:28:50,854 --> 00:28:51,896
Matsuyama,

467
00:28:52,856 --> 00:28:54,941
what were you looking for earlier?

468
00:28:55,024 --> 00:28:57,360
Ah, Nakae's chalk. I felt like

469
00:28:57,444 --> 00:28:59,571
there were fewer boxes
than when I saw them at the booth.

470
00:29:00,363 --> 00:29:01,322
Fewer?

471
00:29:01,990 --> 00:29:04,868
That's what I thought,
but she said it was fine.

472
00:29:05,952 --> 00:29:10,081
Then there shouldn't be a problem.
That concludes our work for today.

473
00:29:10,165 --> 00:29:14,085
Finally heading home.
Ah, what a crazy day.

474
00:29:51,956 --> 00:29:55,210
-Hey, everybody.
-Hello.

475
00:29:55,293 --> 00:30:00,048
The Meyers arrived safely
at the airport from the hotel.

476
00:30:00,131 --> 00:30:03,301
That ends our VIP duty.

477
00:30:03,384 --> 00:30:05,970
We appreciate your cooperation,
more or less.

478
00:30:08,097 --> 00:30:10,266
He actually called it VIP duty…

479
00:30:10,350 --> 00:30:12,519
And he doesn't sound thankful at all.

480
00:30:16,022 --> 00:30:17,398
What are you looking at?

481
00:30:18,149 --> 00:30:21,861
There's something that
has been bugging me.

482
00:30:27,283 --> 00:30:29,452
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

483
00:30:29,536 --> 00:30:31,412
Everyone got some good sleep?

484
00:30:31,496 --> 00:30:33,498
Yes, somehow.

485
00:30:34,374 --> 00:30:37,001
So in the end, no bomb was found.

486
00:30:37,085 --> 00:30:38,711
It seems it was a prank,

487
00:30:40,004 --> 00:30:42,715
almost the same as five years ago.

488
00:30:43,925 --> 00:30:45,134
Um…

489
00:30:47,178 --> 00:30:50,390
What do you mean by "almost the same"?

490
00:30:51,516 --> 00:30:53,935
Was the targeted flight the same as well?

491
00:30:54,018 --> 00:30:54,936
No, not that similar.

492
00:30:56,312 --> 00:30:59,732
This time it was bound for Rome,
but five years ago,

493
00:30:59,816 --> 00:31:04,863
the culprit specified
a flight to Oslo, Norway.

494
00:31:04,946 --> 00:31:06,072
Norway?

495
00:31:06,781 --> 00:31:11,744
The country where the Meyers' daughter
performs music.

496
00:31:11,828 --> 00:31:13,663
<i>Right. Yes, that's right!</i>

497
00:31:17,375 --> 00:31:18,209
What's wrong?

498
00:31:19,544 --> 00:31:24,924
Oh, it's just, Sakura Nakae's
past side job was also in Norway.

499
00:31:25,008 --> 00:31:27,594
<i>-And it was five years ago.</i>
<i>-Nakae too?</i>

500
00:31:27,677 --> 00:31:31,514
Furthermore, Soma's passport travel
history included Norway.

501
00:31:31,598 --> 00:31:32,849
<i>Five years ago as well.</i>

502
00:31:33,391 --> 00:31:35,643
All three of them, in the same country
at the same time…

503
00:31:36,561 --> 00:31:39,063
-Could it be a coincidence?
-Wait a second.

504
00:31:40,231 --> 00:31:43,568
The Meyers' daughter already passed away.

505
00:31:43,651 --> 00:31:44,736
Since when?

506
00:31:45,904 --> 00:31:47,071
Five years ago.

507
00:31:50,366 --> 00:31:55,246
<i>Wait, wait! Does that mean everything</i>
<i>connects back to Norway five years ago?</i>

508
00:31:55,330 --> 00:31:56,789
<i>-The bomb threat,</i>
-Emma…

509
00:31:56,873 --> 00:31:59,292
<i>Sakura Nakae, Soma,</i>

510
00:32:00,251 --> 00:32:01,711
and the Meyers' daughter?

511
00:32:04,380 --> 00:32:05,965
Um…

512
00:32:09,218 --> 00:32:11,846
May I say something as well?

513
00:32:13,848 --> 00:32:17,143
Last night, when we were seeing off
Josef to the hotel,

514
00:32:17,226 --> 00:32:18,978
something felt off to me.

515
00:32:19,812 --> 00:32:22,774
So, I rewatched the footage…

516
00:32:22,857 --> 00:32:23,691
CUSTOMS BOOTH A CAMERA

517
00:32:23,775 --> 00:32:27,403
…and several parts
of the wheelchair were missing.

518
00:32:30,031 --> 00:32:31,574
Pardon us.

519
00:32:33,201 --> 00:32:36,704
-Let me help you.
-Oh, I'm good, thank you. I'm very good.

520
00:32:36,788 --> 00:32:38,289
Parts of the wheelchair?

521
00:32:38,957 --> 00:32:43,419
Yes. And Luisa's pendant
had changed as well.

522
00:32:44,379 --> 00:32:46,839
And you said it earlier too, Matsuyama,

523
00:32:46,923 --> 00:32:48,883
about Sakura Nakae's luggage.

524
00:32:48,967 --> 00:32:52,095
Ah, I felt like the number
of chalk boxes had decreased.

525
00:32:53,054 --> 00:32:57,892
So I extracted the missing items
and assembled them…

526
00:33:02,063 --> 00:33:03,064
and got this.

527
00:33:13,157 --> 00:33:14,242
You dropped this.

528
00:33:22,083 --> 00:33:23,626
Will you come with us?

529
00:33:25,211 --> 00:33:26,295
‎Stand up.

530
00:33:31,175 --> 00:33:33,428
-This is…
-Uh…

531
00:33:34,220 --> 00:33:35,138
What is it?

532
00:33:35,972 --> 00:33:37,348
A gun. It's a gun.

533
00:33:38,599 --> 00:33:41,644
It has a structure close
to a small single-shot pistol.

534
00:33:41,728 --> 00:33:44,856
<i>If so, the bullet</i>
<i>was likely Luisa's pendant.</i>

535
00:33:44,939 --> 00:33:50,278
<i>The gunpowder needed to fire it</i>
<i>was probably mixed into Sakura's chalk.</i>

536
00:34:00,621 --> 00:34:01,456
Get on the phone.

537
00:34:01,539 --> 00:34:02,832
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

538
00:34:05,418 --> 00:34:06,836
-Just this way.
-Thank you.

539
00:34:09,756 --> 00:34:10,923
Wheelchair located!

540
00:34:12,216 --> 00:34:15,303
-Hey, what is this about?
-Shut up.

541
00:34:20,767 --> 00:34:23,352
Do you recognize this girl?

542
00:34:23,436 --> 00:34:26,689
I just got information
from Counselor Sugihara.

543
00:34:26,773 --> 00:34:29,776
<i>The passenger manifest</i>
<i>for the targeted flight</i>

544
00:34:29,859 --> 00:34:32,612
<i>during the bomb scare</i>
<i>five years ago contained</i>

545
00:34:32,695 --> 00:34:34,655
<i>Emma and Soma.</i>

546
00:34:35,239 --> 00:34:40,411
We are currently investigating
what kind of connection there could be.

547
00:34:42,413 --> 00:34:43,498
<i>I met Emma</i>

548
00:34:45,249 --> 00:34:46,959
<i>on a music website.</i>

549
00:34:47,668 --> 00:34:49,378
<i>At first, I was just a fan.</i>

550
00:34:50,129 --> 00:34:51,798
<i>But before I knew it,</i>

551
00:34:52,632 --> 00:34:55,384
we started
contacting each other every day.

552
00:34:57,303 --> 00:34:59,388
That wasn't all, was it?

553
00:35:00,139 --> 00:35:03,392
Sakura truly loved her
from the bottom of her heart.

554
00:35:06,521 --> 00:35:07,688
And Emma

555
00:35:09,232 --> 00:35:10,316
loved her too.

556
00:35:12,026 --> 00:35:14,195
Emma!

557
00:35:15,071 --> 00:35:17,615
<i>Emma was aiming for an international</i>
<i>competition held in Norway.</i>

558
00:35:19,200 --> 00:35:20,701
<i>Winning it</i>

559
00:35:20,785 --> 00:35:22,703
<i>would pave her path</i>
<i>to a prestigious orchestra.</i>

560
00:35:22,787 --> 00:35:24,038
I'm good. How was your flight?

561
00:35:27,708 --> 00:35:29,961
It was the competition
Emma staked her life on.

562
00:35:31,254 --> 00:35:32,922
<i>The day before,</i>

563
00:35:33,005 --> 00:35:35,967
<i>Emma was supposed to transfer</i>
<i>at this airport and head to Norway.</i>

564
00:35:36,050 --> 00:35:37,885
We are currently unable
to board your flight.

565
00:35:37,969 --> 00:35:40,429
But I checked this morning.

566
00:35:40,513 --> 00:35:43,099
-It said it was fine.
-I'm so sorry.

567
00:35:43,724 --> 00:35:44,809
<i>But suddenly,</i>

568
00:35:46,102 --> 00:35:47,812
<i>her flight was canceled.</i>

569
00:35:49,397 --> 00:35:50,231
<i>In the end,</i>

570
00:35:51,607 --> 00:35:53,109
the rescheduled flight was too late.

571
00:35:56,154 --> 00:35:57,655
<i>That wasn't all.</i>

572
00:35:59,532 --> 00:36:01,868
<i>Her precious violin</i>
<i>was stolen at the airport too.</i>

573
00:36:03,786 --> 00:36:07,373
<i>In total shock, Emma was in a daze.</i>

574
00:36:13,171 --> 00:36:14,046
And?

575
00:36:15,089 --> 00:36:16,174
So what?

576
00:36:17,425 --> 00:36:20,511
I feel bad for her,
but what does that have to do with me?

577
00:36:21,304 --> 00:36:23,181
-Bastard...
-Everyone, this way!

578
00:36:24,765 --> 00:36:25,600
‎Go.

579
00:36:33,983 --> 00:36:36,068
-Going there now.
-Roger that.

580
00:36:44,744 --> 00:36:45,786
Found them!

581
00:36:47,288 --> 00:36:49,165
K Area, near the VIP entrance.

582
00:36:52,793 --> 00:36:53,920
Nothing to do with you?

583
00:36:55,671 --> 00:36:57,924
Did you say it has nothing to do with you?

584
00:36:58,007 --> 00:37:01,594
After losing Emma, I went to Norway.

585
00:37:02,720 --> 00:37:05,681
I at least wanted to see
the country she longed for.

586
00:37:06,891 --> 00:37:08,226
I worked in nightlife there too.

587
00:37:09,560 --> 00:37:12,313
Man, that was a close call, seriously.

588
00:37:12,396 --> 00:37:13,856
Did something happen?

589
00:37:13,940 --> 00:37:18,277
Six months ago, I had a huge
business meeting in this country,

590
00:37:18,361 --> 00:37:19,737
but I overslept.

591
00:37:19,820 --> 00:37:22,323
When I woke up,
the plane was about to depart.

592
00:37:22,406 --> 00:37:25,534
-What? That must have been awful.
-Yes.

593
00:37:25,618 --> 00:37:27,745
Normally, it would be game over.

594
00:37:27,828 --> 00:37:30,164
But I'm different.

595
00:37:30,248 --> 00:37:32,333
I made a quick phone call to the airport.

596
00:37:32,416 --> 00:37:34,210
-A phone call?
-Yes.

597
00:37:34,293 --> 00:37:38,881
A magic phone call.
With just one call, I delayed the flight.

598
00:37:39,882 --> 00:37:43,803
Thanks to that, I made it to the plane
and barely made the meeting.

599
00:37:44,804 --> 00:37:47,431
That was brilliant of me, huh?

600
00:37:50,601 --> 00:37:52,895
I wanted you to experience
the exact same thing.

601
00:37:55,022 --> 00:37:56,774
I wanted your flight delayed

602
00:37:58,734 --> 00:38:00,736
so you would lose what matters most.

603
00:38:10,371 --> 00:38:13,582
<i>This is the Information Center</i>
<i>of Kanto International Airport.</i>

604
00:38:14,959 --> 00:38:18,421
A bomb has been planted on the flight
bound for Rome International Airport.

605
00:38:23,884 --> 00:38:26,429
Could it be, my bag too?

606
00:38:28,139 --> 00:38:29,640
Just like Emma.

607
00:38:29,724 --> 00:38:32,101
Like I said, the flight isn't taking off!

608
00:38:33,602 --> 00:38:37,315
Can't you negotiate with them and somehow
push back tomorrow's meeting?

609
00:38:38,441 --> 00:38:39,275
Yes.

610
00:38:39,859 --> 00:38:42,361
I don't know yet.

611
00:38:46,449 --> 00:38:47,575
Stop!

612
00:38:49,368 --> 00:38:50,286
Stop.

613
00:38:51,037 --> 00:38:52,705
Shoot him!

614
00:38:57,877 --> 00:38:59,337
‎I can't do it.

615
00:39:01,797 --> 00:39:02,840
Um…

616
00:39:02,923 --> 00:39:04,675
-Mori, stop!
-Stop!

617
00:39:04,759 --> 00:39:06,761
W-wait! It's my fault!

618
00:39:06,844 --> 00:39:08,637
I was the one
who stopped the plane back then!

619
00:39:08,721 --> 00:39:11,474
But I didn't think
it would turn out like that!

620
00:39:14,185 --> 00:39:15,853
Give Emma back.

621
00:39:26,197 --> 00:39:27,448
Um…

622
00:39:28,991 --> 00:39:32,536
This is the firing pin.
Without this, it won't fire.

623
00:39:42,963 --> 00:39:45,508
Josef, you must already know.

624
00:39:47,968 --> 00:39:52,306
When I assembled it,
I realized the firing pin was missing.

625
00:39:53,182 --> 00:39:55,434
-But…
-All we wanted from this man

626
00:39:55,518 --> 00:39:57,269
was an apology to Emma.

627
00:40:00,481 --> 00:40:01,607
Where was it?

628
00:40:02,691 --> 00:40:04,819
At Gate 24.

629
00:40:04,902 --> 00:40:06,070
What?

630
00:40:10,282 --> 00:40:11,534
What's wrong with you?

631
00:40:22,294 --> 00:40:23,546
That was it?

632
00:40:37,101 --> 00:40:40,020
‎I think Emma probably stopped us

633
00:40:40,104 --> 00:40:43,691
‎-from doing something foolish.
‎-That's right.

634
00:41:15,181 --> 00:41:17,683
I could have died!

635
00:41:17,766 --> 00:41:20,644
Because your airport security was lacking!

636
00:41:22,855 --> 00:41:23,814
Hey!

637
00:41:26,609 --> 00:41:30,196
Excuse me. I am Sugihara.

638
00:41:31,405 --> 00:41:34,867
We are truly sorry for the trouble caused.

639
00:41:34,950 --> 00:41:39,455
Absolutely! In the end, I couldn't
even attend my important meeting.

640
00:41:40,664 --> 00:41:44,210
I'm going to claim damages for this.

641
00:41:44,293 --> 00:41:46,545
Is that so? Against whom?

642
00:41:47,171 --> 00:41:48,088
Huh?

643
00:41:48,172 --> 00:41:50,925
The bomb threat five years ago,

644
00:41:51,008 --> 00:41:54,136
voiceprint analysis and call records
from that time confirmed

645
00:41:55,304 --> 00:41:59,141
it was your doing, Mr. Soma.

646
00:42:01,435 --> 00:42:03,729
The statute of limitations
for this matter has not expired yet.

647
00:42:04,605 --> 00:42:07,608
You may face prosecution
for fraudulent obstruction of business

648
00:42:07,691 --> 00:42:10,444
and attempted extortion.

649
00:42:10,528 --> 00:42:11,737
Um…

650
00:42:11,820 --> 00:42:16,700
In addition, the airport plans to file
a claim for damages against you.

651
00:42:16,784 --> 00:42:19,495
At least in the hundreds
of millions of yen.

652
00:42:19,578 --> 00:42:23,624
That is the gravity of what you did.

653
00:42:32,550 --> 00:42:33,759
A BOOTH - B BOOTH - PLANTS AND ANIMALS
CUSTOMS - MOBILE PERSONNEL

654
00:42:33,842 --> 00:42:35,010
SCHEDULED FLIGHTS

655
00:42:35,094 --> 00:42:36,220
BRISBANE - PANAMA CITY
SHANGHAI - BARCELONA

656
00:42:39,265 --> 00:42:40,849
Is something wrong?

657
00:42:41,976 --> 00:42:43,102
I must confess.

658
00:42:43,185 --> 00:42:46,897
I missed the weapons being brought in.

659
00:42:47,565 --> 00:42:49,692
If we're talking about that,
then so did I.

660
00:42:49,775 --> 00:42:53,237
Me too. It's really frustrating.

661
00:42:53,320 --> 00:42:55,698
But asking anyone to spot that
would be impossible, right?

662
00:42:55,781 --> 00:42:57,241
It couldn't be helped.

663
00:42:57,825 --> 00:43:00,286
It was impossible. It couldn't be helped.

664
00:43:01,996 --> 00:43:03,914
Is it really okay to excuse it like that?

665
00:43:04,873 --> 00:43:06,500
You didn't spot it either.

666
00:43:06,584 --> 00:43:08,919
No, like I said, I--

667
00:43:09,003 --> 00:43:12,673
-Now, now, both of you!
-Fighting again?

668
00:43:14,133 --> 00:43:15,593
Counselor Sugihara.

669
00:43:15,676 --> 00:43:18,929
Thank you so much
for your hard work, everyone.

670
00:43:19,013 --> 00:43:23,392
But in the future, please be mindful
of what our team's name means.

671
00:43:24,143 --> 00:43:26,812
-Our team's name?
-Gate 24?

672
00:43:26,895 --> 00:43:29,690
Come to think of it,
I've wondered for a while.

673
00:43:29,773 --> 00:43:32,318
What does 24 mean?

674
00:43:32,401 --> 00:43:36,780
Does it mean a gate that responds
to any situation 24 hours a day?

675
00:43:38,407 --> 00:43:40,659
That was certainly true this time.

676
00:43:41,660 --> 00:43:43,120
But there is another meaning.

677
00:43:44,413 --> 00:43:45,539
Two times four.

678
00:43:46,248 --> 00:43:47,958
Two times four?

679
00:43:48,042 --> 00:43:49,335
Eight?

680
00:43:49,418 --> 00:43:50,919
No, that's not it.

681
00:43:51,003 --> 00:43:56,592
It means evaluating both people
and objects through the four perspectives

682
00:43:56,675 --> 00:43:59,178
of Immigration, Customs,
Quarantine, and Police.

683
00:43:59,261 --> 00:44:03,849
This team is a gathering of people
with different positions.

684
00:44:05,309 --> 00:44:06,393
However,

685
00:44:07,394 --> 00:44:10,022
precisely because each of you
has a different perspective,

686
00:44:11,023 --> 00:44:12,274
there are things only you can notice.

687
00:44:13,942 --> 00:44:18,572
That is the true strength of Gate 24.

688
00:44:19,490 --> 00:44:21,283
So, everybody,

689
00:44:22,159 --> 00:44:24,995
try to get along a little better.

690
00:44:27,998 --> 00:44:29,375
Oh my…

691
00:44:37,675 --> 00:44:40,928
PLANTS AND ANIMALS INSPECTION

692
00:44:46,141 --> 00:44:48,686
‎-<i>‎My son was kidnapped.</i>
‎-<i>‎Kidnapped…</i>

693
00:44:48,769 --> 00:44:50,604
<i>‎We lost track of an animal,</i>
<i>‎which we must monitor,</i>

694
00:44:50,687 --> 00:44:52,898
<i>‎and a child, who we must protect,</i>
<i>‎at the same time!</i>

695
00:44:52,981 --> 00:44:54,566
<i>‎I made a mistake at a critical time.</i>

696
00:44:54,650 --> 00:44:55,526
<i>‎Hayami!</i>

697
00:44:56,944 --> 00:44:59,071
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman
